=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
issue: 213
title: bumping a setup action inside a composite action is a CI edit, not a weakening
origin: issue #213: every edit to a composite action definition is reported at warn, as a workflow edit is
=== before: .github/actions/setup/action.yml ===
name: test
description: run the test suite
runs:
  using: composite
  steps:
    - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
      with:
        python-version: "3.12"
    - run: pip install -e .[test]
      shell: bash
    - run: pytest
      shell: bash
=== after: .github/actions/setup/action.yml ===
name: test
description: run the test suite
runs:
  using: composite
  steps:
    - uses: actions/setup-python@v6
      with:
        python-version: "3.12"
    - run: pip install -e .[test]
      shell: bash
    - run: pytest
      shell: bash
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
